Predictive Maintenance Platform for Higher Aircraft Availability
Abstract

Aircraft maintenance plays a crucial role in ensuring flight safety, operational reliability, and fleet availability. Traditional maintenance approaches, such as scheduled and reactive maintenance, may lead to unnecessary component replacements, unexpected equipment failures, increased maintenance costs, and aircraft downtime. To address these challenges, this project proposes a Predictive Maintenance Platform for Higher Aircraft Availability that leverages aircraft sensor data, machine learning, and data analytics to predict potential component failures before they occur.

The proposed platform collects and processes aircraft operational and sensor data, including temperature, vibration, pressure, operating hours, and other relevant health indicators. Machine learning algorithms are used to identify abnormal operating patterns, estimate component degradation, and predict possible maintenance requirements. The platform can also provide equipment health monitoring, failure-risk alerts, maintenance recommendations, and an interactive dashboard to support maintenance planning and decision-making.

By enabling condition-based maintenance and early fault detection, the system aims to minimize unexpected aircraft ground time, optimize maintenance schedules, improve resource utilization, and reduce overall maintenance expenses. Historical maintenance records and sensor measurements can be analyzed to identify recurring failure patterns and improve predictive performance over time.

The proposed solution provides a data-driven approach to aircraft health management, supporting the transition from conventional maintenance practices toward intelligent and proactive maintenance planning. The expected outcome is improved aircraft availability, enhanced operational efficiency, and more reliable maintenance decisions. The platform can be further extended with real-time data integration and scalable analytics to support fleet-level monitoring.

Keywords: Predictive Maintenance, Aircraft Availability, Machine Learning, Aircraft Health Monitoring, Fault Detection, Sensor Data Analytics, Remaining Useful Life (RUL), Condition-Based Maintenance.
